{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":45.220001220703125,"text":"People in Thessaloniki just call it the Camara, and it is the city's most common meeting point at the Camara, at 6. It was built around AD 299 to celebrate a victory of the emperor Galerius. It was not originally one arch, but a large structure with eight piers and four openings, and only a part of it survives. The piers carry marble panels carved in bands, like a comic strip, read from the bottom upwards. Soldiers, horses, elephants, ambassadors. What matters most is where it stood. The Via Egnatia ran underneath it, the Roman road that started on the Adriatic and ran all the way to Byzantium. Anyone traveling from Rome towards the east came through here. The route still exists. Egnatia Street runs right past it.","words":[{"word":"People","start":0,"end":0.5799999833106995},{"word":"in","start":0.5799999833106995,"end":0.9200000166893005},{"word":"Thessaloniki","start":0.9200000166893005,"end":1.399999976158142},{"word":"just","start":1.399999976158142,"end":1.899999976158142},{"word":"call","start":1.899999976158142,"end":2.119999885559082},{"word":"it","start":2.119999885559082,"end":2.2799999713897705},{"word":"the","start":2.2799999713897705,"end":2.759999990463257},{"word":"Camara","start":2.759999990463257,"end":2.9800000190734863},{"word":"and","start":3.5399999618530273,"end":3.619999885559082},{"word":"it","start":3.619999885559082,"end":3.7200000286102295},{"word":"is","start":3.7200000286102295,"end":3.880000114440918},{"word":"the","start":3.880000114440918,"end":4.119999885559082},{"word":"city's","start":4.119999885559082,"end":4.400000095367432},{"word":"most","start":4.400000095367432,"end":4.699999809265137},{"word":"common","start":4.699999809265137,"end":5.039999961853027},{"word":"meeting","start":5.039999961853027,"end":5.360000133514404},{"word":"point","start":5.360000133514404,"end":5.659999847412109},{"word":"at","start":5.659999847412109,"end":6.13999986648559